// Allocation-attribution fixture (attribution category, D-385/D-386): array
// member dispatch plus array growth. Same 1,000-iteration shape as
// attr-native.grob, but the native call is xs.append(i) instead of "x".upper(),
// which also grows the backing GrobArray via doubling.
//
// Subtract attr-array-dispatch.grob, not attr-native.grob, to isolate growth:
// append and contains share the GetProperty binding path, whereas upper is a
// registered Stdlib-plugin native on a structurally cheaper path (phase 1 §4).
// attr-build minus attr-native gives combined dispatch-tax-plus-growth cost.
xs: int[] := []
for i in 1..1000 {
    xs.append(i)
}
